\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Constructed an explicit homogeneous Euclidean four-point diagnostic failing inversion covariance; identified the additional Ward identities needed for the source fermionic fixed point.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the supplied definition, catalogue wording, source qualifications and reference entries for 30005177. The historical source/context and inherited status are retained; no fresh literature or novelty certification is claimed. No external theorem is used without proof in this attempt; explicit model assumptions are distinguished from facts about the source model.

\paragraph{A scale-to-conformal diagnostic.} For distinct nonzero Euclidean points define the scalar four-point expression
\[
 F(x_1,x_2,x_3,x_4)=|x_1-x_2|^{-2\Delta}|x_3-x_4|^{-2\Delta}
 \left(1+\varepsilon\frac{|x_1-x_2|}{|x_3-x_4|}\right),\qquad\varepsilon\ne0.
\]
It is translation and rotation invariant and homogeneous of degree \(-4\Delta\). Under inversion \(I(x)=x/|x|^2\), direct squaring proves \(|I(x)-I(y)|=|x-y|/(|x||y|)\). The first product therefore acquires the expected factor \(\prod_j|x_j|^{2\Delta}\), but the additional ratio acquires \(|x_3||x_4|/(|x_1||x_2|)\), which is generally not one. Thus the expression fails the corresponding primary-field inversion law despite its scale covariance.
\paragraph{The actual missing identity.} In a fixed-point proof one must establish special-conformal identities as well as dilation identities. For scalar primary components this includes vanishing of the sum of generators \(2x_j^\mu x_j\cdot\partial_{x_j}-|x_j|^2\partial_{x_j^\mu}+2\Delta x_j^\mu\) acting on the correlation, with the appropriate spin/internal terms in the fermionic case.
\paragraph{Scope audit.} The diagnostic expression is not claimed to be a consistent fermionic correlation hierarchy or the source fixed point. It refutes an insufficient symmetry inference only. The first gap is deriving the full conformal Ward identities for the actual non-Gaussian long-range symplectic model, controlling nonlocal kernels and anomalies. No proof that scale invariance fails there, and no conformal-invariance result, is supplied.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked inversion distance factors and scale degree; distinguished a symmetry diagnostic from a valid fermionic correlation hierarchy or counterexample. This is a GPT-6 Astra Ultra self-audit, not independent human verification. Prompt A drafting followed by prompt B scope/dependency/boundary self-audit. Checked inversion distance factors and scale degree; distinguished a symmetry diagnostic from a valid fermionic correlation hierarchy or counterexample. The remaining gap is: Prove the special-conformal Ward identities with nonlocal and fermionic terms for the actual interacting fixed-point correlations. Unresolved status and zero original-target completion are retained.

Coordinator checked the inversion distance identity and failure of the extra ratio to have primary-field covariance. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 and local file-reading/writing tools for manuscript serialization and structural checks; mathematical calculations were symbolic reasoning, with no numerical experiment or theorem prover. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

\paragraph{Final status and first remaining gap.}
\textbf{UNRESOLVED}. Prove the special-conformal Ward identities with nonlocal and fermionic terms for the actual interacting fixed-point correlations.

